      "writtenOn": "2023-05-30T22:24:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I consider having these constants defined here to be problematic for two reasons:\n\n1. They define an implementation-specific constant which becomes visible to anyone who includes this header. So for example, another unrelated module which for some reason ends up including this header will get `kDefaultFormat`, and it may easily clash with a constant of the same name used by that module. Usually when defining an internal constant in a header file can\u0027t be avoided, it must be defined in some nested namespace.\n\n2. Having a non-static non-primitive constant in a header file can easily lead to an ODR violation (https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/definition). I understand that we can\u0027t make it a `constexpr` because it contains a string, so...\n\nSince these constants seem to be used by code in this module, and `AudioConfig` is used by value, thus it has to be defined here, one way to make things proper is to declare these constants inside `AudioConfig` as `static` members. For non-constexpr constants, we also have to define them in `StreamRouteSubmix.cpp` (https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/static#Constant_static_members).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9ab252a6790e0961468f87e9fc0e3133309463af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
